# Committed data files MUST NOT be line-ending translated.
#
# On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows' installer
# default), git rewrites LF -> CRLF on checkout for anything it considers
# text -- which includes .json and .csv. Anything that hashes or compares
# their exact bytes then fails, with nothing in the error pointing at the
# cause.
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending translation in both directions, so the
# bytes in the working tree are always the committed bytes.
*.json -text
*.csv  -text
